@namespace Beastborne.UI.Components
@using System;
@using System.Collections.Generic;
@using Sandbox;
@using Sandbox.UI;
@using Beastborne.UI;
@using Beastborne.UI.Primitives;
@using Beastborne.Systems;
@inherits Panel

@*
    PhoneLauncher v3 — the PawPad, running TamerLink OS (player-facing
    branding only; code identity stays PhoneLauncher). The phone-shaped
    navigation launcher (Fable 5 sweep, guiding-star §Navigation).
    Summoned by the MENU button / Slot8; the persistent bottom bar stays
    mounted for now (A/B trial — retirement comes after the user blesses
    the phone).

    v4 (live screenshot feedback — "sell the DEVICE"):
    - HIGHLIGHT BARS REMOVED (user dislikes) — the gold→violet energy
      hairline is deleted and the header's gold accent rule is switched
      off (AccentWidth 0 in markup + display:none in our scss — a 0-width
      div can still render as an artifact; empty-div quirk). The title
      breathes on its own.
    - REAL BEZEL — .pl-shell wraps the screen: near-black frame (r-38
      outer / screen keeps r-30; 10px sides, 20px top strip, 12px chin),
      speaker slit + camera lens centered in the top strip, two side-
      button nubs on the LEFT (receding) edge. Footprint 576px wide incl.
      bezel — every doctrine width recomputed: screen content 512, tiles
      160, gaps 16 (rows sum 512 exactly). Shadow/lean/entrance unchanged.
    - LABELS RE-CENTERED, v4.1 FINAL (v4's main-axis-width theory was
      DISPROVEN live: the 160px/392px boxes held, yet the text still drew
      left — text-align is a NO-OP under the leaned ancestor, because the
      transform poisons derived width resolution and the Label's inner
      text box collapses to content width; nothing to align within).
      Fix: centering BY CONSTRUCTION — auto-width spans + razor-computed
      margin-left (LabelPadPx/NamePadPx, calibrated glyph estimates).
      Doctrine: inside a transformed subtree, only explicit px layout
      exists; text-align does not.
    - AVATAR (screenshot: no circle) — the command bar's cb-avatar recipe
      copied VERBATIM (fallback emoji span + absolute 50%+negative-half-
      margin img — cb's comment says flex-centering shifts images), then
      cosmetics adapted to a 22px circle with a 2px violet rim. One-shot
      [pawpad] log of the resolved src fires on first visible frame so
      the next session can diagnose from the log if it's STILL missing.
    - HINTS REBUILT (screenshot: WASD wrapped to "WA/SD"; ENTER cap an
      empty gold blob) — the caps were sized under their text (32px for
      4 chars) with auto-width spans centered by justify-content (zero-
      width anchor under the lean). Every cap AND its inner span now
      carry explicit widths + white-space: nowrap; ENTER's dark GoldInk
      on gold verified in the scss.
    - FPS FIX (live: 7fps open / 43-87 closed) — the ring's per-frame
      ink-lean wave (`Style.Transform` write EVERY frame on an element
      INSIDE the perspective-leaned device) re-dirtied the whole leaned
      subtree each frame and forced a full 3D re-composite. THE WAVE IS
      RETIRED on the PawPad (the menu keeps its waving cursor at ROOT
      level, outside its tilted panels — that's why it's cheap there).
      Ring rect math is now EVENT-DRIVEN (_ringDirty on open/focus move,
      not per-frame), and ClockText is cached (refreshed ≤1/s) so
      BuildHash isn't allocating a DateTime string per frame. Target:
      zero measurable per-frame work while open and idle.
    - ANCHOR HARDENED (live: only a ~40px sliver at the right edge) —
      the root placed the AUTO-width .pl-wrap with justify-content:
      flex-end — the doctrine's zero-width-anchor pattern at the one
      scope it hadn't been applied to. .pl-wrap and .pl-device now carry
      explicit width 576px so flex-end sums a real number. (The sliver
      was possibly also mid-edit hotload — the shell div briefly existed
      with no scss — but the explicit widths make the anchor lawful
      either way.)

    v3.1 (live-test feedback + "make it actually look good" pass):
    - SWEEP BUG ROOT-CAUSED — log-proven: every MAIN APP took the widget
      branch ("[sweepdbg] widget launch 'beasts'"). The record flag was
      renamed Liquid→Sweep in v2, and s&box hotload migrates STATIC data
      across recompiles by copying record members BY NAME — no name match,
      so every migrated PhoneApp got Sweep=default(false), and every later
      hotload faithfully copied the stale false forward. Fix: destination
      vs widget is now classified IN CODE (IsWidgetApp — method bodies are
      always fresh after hotload; only DATA can go stale). The Sweep field
      is deleted so nothing misleading remains. ⚠ Never rename fields in
      the PhoneApp record without expecting a full-restart requirement.
    - RIGHT-SIDE ANCHOR — the phone lives at the right edge (72px in,
      vertically centered) so the game stays visible; entrance is a
      slide-in from the right edge, exit mirrors. Backdrop dim lightened
      to 0.55 — seeing the game behind is now the point.
    - THE LEAN FLIPPED — perspective(1600px) rotateY(-13deg), origin
      right center (the PawPad mockup's values): right side toward the
      camera, left recedes, sold by a left-edge shade overlay + the
      energy hairline along the top edge (device is "on").
    - FOCUS POP — the focused icon lifts toward the player
      (translateY(-4px) scale(1.06), 0.12s) and the living ring RIDES the
      lift: Box.Rect doesn't move with CSS transforms, so UpdateRing
      mirrors the pop into the ring's target rect (the menu's SelectedPop
      lockstep). Press settles back down to scale(0.98) inside the ring.
    - HEADER v2 — PROTOTYPE stamp deleted; status row gains signal bars;
      TAMERLINK OS eyebrow in violet over a 34px italic PawPad with the
      gold accent rule (BbSectionHeader, KickerColor override); Steam
      avatar (command-bar house pattern) beside the tamer line.
    - DOCTRINE TIGHTENED (live: EXPEDITION's label row overran its tile
      and clipped the body edge) — justify-content placement of AUTO-width
      children drifts too, not just space-between/align-items. Labels are
      now single full-width text-align: center spans; keycaps ride the
      icon corner as fixed absolutes; the hints/status rows give every
      child an explicit width. Full strict doctrine in the SCSS header.

    v3 (live-test feedback):
    - THE LIVING RING — the per-tile static rings are dead; ONE violet
      cursor ring (the main menu's signature) glides between focused
      icons on the 0.27s signature ease, with the ink-lean wave running
      per-frame (menu's multi-sine at 60% amplitude). It lives INSIDE
      .pl-grid, so it shares the device's 3D lean with the icons —
      flat Box.Rect delta math positions it, no perspective compensation
      needed (unlike MainMenu's tilted-panel cursor). Snaps on open
      (warmup frames), glides thereafter.
    - ALIGNMENT HARDENED — v2 drifted right in-engine: auto-width flex
      children placed by align-items/space-between landed as if their
      width were zero (labels started at the icon's center and ran right;
      the stamp/LV line ran off the body edge). Fix: every centered or
      right-anchored box now has an EXPLICIT width; centering is done by
      justify-content inside fixed boxes or hard margins, never by
      cross-axis auto placement. Absolute badges get explicit widths
      (width:auto never shrink-wraps an absolute element — quirk).
    - SWEEP_DEBUG — temp per-phase Log.Info proving the accent swipe
      runs (SWAP_DEBUG precedent). Flip false once verified live.

    The phone is a ROUTER, not content: a 3×4 grid of "app" icons, one per
    destination. v2 (live feedback): apps look like APPS — each is an 88px
    rounded square FILLED SOLID with its accent color (the color IS the
    icon; the launcher grid is the one sanctioned full-rainbow surface),
    glyph centered, label below. Tapping an app plays THE ACCENT SWIPE:
    a full-screen angled slab in the app's accent sweeps across the screen
    (the menu→game Persona-wipe vocabulary, single accent, phone-speed),
    NavManager routes at full cover, the slab sweeps off the far side.

    Juice-tier discipline: the swipe plays for DESTINATIONS (the 6 tabs +
    Quests + Bag — full-screen contexts). The four widget apps
    (Chat/Radio/Effects/Notifications) just close the phone and toggle
    their popup — a fullscreen accent sweep to open a chat widget would
    be Tier-4 juice on a Tier-1 action.

    Engine rules honored (css-quirks.md):
    - Root PARKS OFFSCREEN when closed (left -10000px, never display-flip).
    - Backdrop uses top/left + width/height 100% — all-edge absolute
      stretching resolves to ZERO SIZE on an empty element.
    - 3D lean holder (.pl-device) carries NO bg/border — the painted
      device lives on a direct child (.pl-shell, screen inside it).
    - Swipe slab = solid div; position/size/translate/skew are IMPERATIVE
      per-frame Style writes (class-toggle transforms snap; per-frame
      re-assert survives any mid-cover rebuild — the held-tween lesson).
    - Slab geometry converts Box.Rect screen px → style px via
      ScaleFromScreen (+30% oversize) so cover is guaranteed at any
      window scale (the liquid circle under-covered without this).
    - Icon children are pointer-events: none (hover-flicker rule).

    Keyboard (registered with UIModalState as "PhoneLauncher"):
    WASD walk the grid · Enter/Space launch · number keys + T/R/C/N route
    directly to their app · Q/Esc/Slot8 close. Hover == focus (one cursor).
*@

<root class="phone-root @(Shown ? "shown" : "") @(IsVisible ? "open" : "") @(_fx != FxPhase.Idle ? "fx-live" : "")">
    <div class="pl-backdrop" onclick=@OnBackdropClicked></div>

    <div class="pl-wrap">
        <div class="pl-device" @ref="_deviceRef">
            <!-- Side-button nubs — LEFT edge (the far/receding side under
                 the rotateY(-13deg) lean). Absolute children of the
                 UN-painted lean holder (the behind-parent-bg quirk only
                 bites when the parent paints its own fill). DOM-before
                 the shell so the shell's rounded edge covers their 1px
                 tuck-under. Explicit boxes throughout. -->
            <div class="pl-nub nub-a"></div>
            <div class="pl-nub nub-b"></div>

            <!-- THE SHELL — the physical device: near-black bezel frame,
                 r-38 outer. Speaker slit + camera lens live in the top
                 strip; the old surface becomes the SCREEN inside (r-30).
                 The shell is a CHILD of the transform holder, so its
                 bg/shadow project correctly with the 3D lean (only the
                 holder's OWN fills render flat — quirk). -->
            <div class="pl-shell">
                <div class="pl-bezel-top">
                    <div class="pl-speaker"></div>
                    <div class="pl-camera"><div class="pl-camera-lens"></div></div>
                </div>

                <div class="pl-surface">
                <!-- Status row: clock · signal bars · tamer line + [avatar].
                     Light — the phone routes, it doesn't inform. Bars are
                     four explicit fixed-size divs (ascending, last one dim
                     — "3 of 4"). The identity pair is drift-proof: the name
                     is a right-aligned EXPLICIT-width span whose right edge
                     lands flush against the fixed avatar (children's widths
                     sum to the container exactly — no justify-content
                     placement of auto-width boxes anywhere in this row).
                     Avatar sources exactly like the command bar: Steam
                     avatar: URL, gendered portrait PNG fallback. -->
                <div class="pl-top">
                    <span class="pl-clock">@ClockText</span>
                    <div class="pl-sig">
                        <div class="pl-sig-bar b1"></div>
                        <div class="pl-sig-bar b2"></div>
                        <div class="pl-sig-bar b3"></div>
                        <div class="pl-sig-bar b4"></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pl-id">
                        <span class="pl-lv" style="margin-left: @(NamePadPx())px;">@TamerLine</span>
                        <!-- v4.2: the GUILD roster's avatar recipe (user
                             pointer — the one that provably paints):
                             a PLAIN IN-FLOW img with explicit px size +
                             border-radius, no absolute + 50% centering
                             (50%-derived offsets are poisoned under the
                             lean, same family as the dead text-align).
                             Rim lives on the img itself. -->
                        @if ( GetSteamId() > 0 )
                        {
                            <img class="pl-ava-steam" src="avatar:@GetSteamId()" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <img class="pl-ava-steam" src="@GetAvatarImagePath()" />
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Title block: violet TAMERLINK OS eyebrow + 34px italic
                     PawPad. v4: the gold accent rule is OFF (user dislikes
                     the bars) — width 0 here, display:none in our scss
                     (belt + braces: a 0-width div can still render as an
                     artifact panel; empty-div quirk). -->
                <div class="pl-head">
                    <!-- v4.2: the PawPad mark — a violet app-tile-miniature
                         with a gold paw glyph, left of the title block.
                         Explicit px throughout (lean law). -->
                    <div class="pl-logo">
                        <iconify icon="lucide:paw-print" Size=@(26) Color="#ffce3a" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="pl-head-text">
                        <BbSectionHeader Kicker="TAMERLINK OS" Title="PawPad" Size=@(34) KickerColor="#9b6cff" AccentWidthIdle=@(0) AccentWidthFlare=@(0) />
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="pl-grid" @ref="_gridRef">
                    @for ( int r = 0; r < 4; r++ )
                    {
                        <div class="pl-row">
                            @for ( int c = 0; c < 3; c++ )
                            {
                                var i = r * 3 + c;
                                var app = Apps[i];
                                var badge = GetBadgeCount( app.Id );
                                <div class="pl-app @(i == _kb ? "focused" : "")"
                                     onclick=@(() => LaunchIndex( i ))
                                     onmouseover=@(() => HoverTile( i ))>
                                    <div class="pl-app-iconwrap">
                                        <!-- Offset shadow is ALWAYS present (value-swap on focus,
                                             never add/remove: s&box doesn't clear a REMOVED inline
                                             style property — a dropped box-shadow ghosts forever).
                                             v5.2 (user call): on focus the SHADOW STAYS PLANTED and
                                             the tile lifts off it — box-shadow travels with the
                                             element, so the focused offset adds the lift distance
                                             back (y: 5 + FocusPopLift 6 = 11) to appear anchored. -->
                                        <div class="pl-app-icon" style="background-color: @(i == _kb ? Brighten( app.Accent ) : app.Accent); box-shadow: @(i == _kb ? "3px 11px" : "3px 5px") 0px @(Darken( app.Accent ));">
                                            <!-- v5: the commissioned icon set (Claude Design,
                                                 icons/v2) — filled-silhouette SVGs that carry
                                                 their own fill color (white; dark ink baked in
                                                 for shop/effects), so DarkGlyph stays data-only.
                                                 The PhoneApp.Icon lucide id is retired but the
                                                 FIELD stays: hotload migrates static records BY
                                                 NAME and shape changes force restarts. -->
                                            <img class="pl-app-glyph" src="ui/icons/pawpad/@(app.Id).svg" />
                                        </div>
                                        <!-- v5.1: corner keycaps REMOVED (user: "just in the
                                             way"). The hotkeys still WORK — they're just not
                                             printed on every tile anymore. -->
                                        @if ( app.Id == "bag" && HasNewItems() )
                                        {
                                            <BbStamp Text="NEW" Tone="gold" Tilt=@(3) Class="pl-new-stamp" />
                                        }
                                        else if ( badge > 0 )
                                        {
                                            <span class="pl-badge @(app.DarkGlyph ? "dark-ink" : "")" style="background-color: @app.Accent;">@FormatBadge( badge )</span>
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                    <!-- v4.1: centering BY CONSTRUCTION. Live capture proved
                                         text-align is a no-op anywhere under the lean: the
                                         transformed ancestor poisons derived width resolution
                                         (the documented translate(-50%) flex-poison law), so
                                         the Label's inner text box collapses to content width
                                         and there is nothing to center within — even when the
                                         span's own 160px main-axis box HOLDS (proven by the
                                         avatar landing flush right of .pl-lv's held 392px).
                                         Only explicit px survive in here: auto-width span
                                         (content-collapse now works FOR us) + computed
                                         margin-left. -->
                                    <div class="pl-app-labelrow">
                                        <span class="pl-app-label" style="margin-left: @(LabelPadPx( app.Label ))px;">@app.Label</span>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }

                </div>

                <!-- THE SYSTEM DOCK (v5) — meta destinations (Profile /
                     Settings / Guide / Feedback) as a quieter tier below
                     the grid: smaller dark-violet tiles, violet glyphs
                     (system chrome, not apps). No labels — dock convention;
                     the ring + glyphs carry it. Indices 12-15 in the one
                     cursor space. justify-content: center is LEGAL here:
                     every child is an explicit 56px box (doctrine rule 2). -->
                <div class="pl-dock" @ref="_dockRef">
                    @for ( int d = 0; d < Dock.Length; d++ )
                    {
                        var di = GridCount + d;
                        var dockId = Dock[d];
                        <div class="pl-dock-app @(di == _kb ? "focused" : "")"
                             onclick=@(() => LaunchIndex( di ))
                             onmouseover=@(() => HoverTile( di ))>
                            <img class="pl-dock-glyph" src="ui/icons/pawpad/@(dockId).svg" />
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Receding-side shade — a SIBLING of the shell (absolute
                 children paint BEHIND a panel's own background fill —
                 engine quirk — so it must sit beside the painted shell,
                 not inside it). DOM order paints it above; pointer-events
                 none. The v3.1 energy hairline is DELETED (v4 user call). -->
            <div class="pl-shade"></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- THE LIVING RING — one violet cursor for the whole grid (menu
         signature). v4.2: RELOCATED to ROOT level, OUTSIDE the leaned
         subtree — the menu's own placement, and the fix for BOTH v4
         regressions at once: (1) per-frame wave writes are cheap again
         (they no longer dirty the 3D device — the 7fps law), so the
         liquid ink-lean is BACK; (2) position comes straight from the
         icons' PROJECTED screen rects, so the ring centers exactly on
         every column (the old in-lean delta math assumed uniform scale,
         but perspective compresses the far/left side more — the ring
         drifted sideways on left/middle columns, user-reported).
         left/top/w/h via markup style (CSS transitions glide), wave via
         imperative Style.Transform per frame (never re-renders). -->
    <div @ref="_ringRef" class="pl-cursor @(_ringWarmup >= 2 ? "" : "snap")"
         style="left: @(_ringL)px; top: @(_ringT)px; width: @(_ringW)px; height: @(_ringH)px;"></div>

    <!-- THE ACCENT SWIPE slab — solid accent fill, driven entirely
         imperatively from StepFx(). Sits AFTER .pl-wrap so it paints over
         the phone. pointer-events: none — input outruns animation. -->
    <div class="pl-swipe" @ref="_swipe" style="background-color: @_fxAccent;"></div>
</root>

@code {
    // ── Static show/hide API (the house pattern: static IsVisible + BuildHash) ──

    public static PhoneLauncher Instance { get; private set; }

    /// <summary>True while the phone UI is open (UIModalState reads this).</summary>
    public static bool IsVisible { get; private set; }

    // Close animation window — the root stays on-screen (parked-open) until
    // this expires so the reverse transition is visible before parking.
    private static float _closingUntil;

    public static void Show()
    {
        if ( IsVisible ) return;
        IsVisible = true;
        _closingUntil = 0f;
        SoundManager.PlayPopup();
        Instance?.ResetForOpen();
    }

    public static void Close()
    {
        if ( !IsVisible ) return;
        IsVisible = false;
        _closingUntil = Time.Now + 0.18f;
        SoundManager.PlayPopdown();
    }

    public static void Toggle()
    {
        if ( IsVisible ) Close();
        else Show();
    }

    // ── App registry — grid order (3 cols × 4 rows) ─────────────────────
    // Each destination owns ONE accent (guiding-star three-color identity:
    // that token drives the icon fill, the badge, and the accent swipe).
    //
    // ⚠ HOTLOAD DATA-STALENESS LAW (learned the hard way): this array is
    // static, and s&box hotload MIGRATES static data across recompiles by
    // copying record members BY NAME — the initializer never re-runs. When
    // v2 renamed the `Liquid` flag to `Sweep`, every live session's
    // migrated PhoneApp got Sweep=default(false) and EVERY destination
    // silently took the widget branch (log-proven: "[sweepdbg] widget
    // launch 'beasts'"). Rules: (1) behavior BRANCHES live in code
    // (IsWidgetApp below), never in migrated data; (2) never rename a
    // field in this record without expecting stale values until a full
    // editor restart.
    private record PhoneApp( string Id, string Label, string Icon, string Accent, string Key, bool IsTab, string RouteId, bool DarkGlyph );

    private static readonly PhoneApp[] Apps =
    {
        // Row 1 — the core loop
        new( "beasts",      "BEASTS",     "lucide:paw-print",      "#7b4ddb", "1", true,  "monsters",   false ),
        new( "skills",      "SKILLS",     "lucide:network",        "#ff6bd6", "2", true,  "skills",     false ),
        new( "expedition",  "EXPEDITION", "lucide:map",            "#ee5421", "3", true,  "expedition", false ),
        // Row 2 — the world
        new( "online",      "ONLINE",     "lucide:globe",          "#3f8fe0", "4", true,  "online",     false ),
        new( "beastbook",   "BEASTBOOK",  "lucide:book-open",      "#2dd4bf", "5", true,  "beastiary",  false ),
        new( "shop",        "SHOP",       "lucide:shopping-bag",   "#ffce3a", "6", true,  "shop",       true ),
        // Row 3 — your stuff
        new( "quests",      "QUESTS",     "lucide:scroll-text",    "#3fb45e", "7", false, NavManager.OverlayQuests, false ),
        new( "bag",         "BAG",        "lucide:backpack",       "#d9a054", "9", false, NavManager.OverlayBag,    false ),
        new( "chat",        "CHAT",       "lucide:message-circle", "#4aa8ff", "T", false, NavManager.OverlayChat,   false ),
        // Row 4 — the widgets
        new( "radio",       "RADIO",      "lucide:radio",          "#c26bff", "R", false, NavManager.OverlayRadio,         false ),
        new( "effects",     "EFFECTS",    "lucide:sparkles",       "#f7e024", "C", false, NavManager.OverlayEffects,       true ),
        new( "alerts",      "ALERTS",     "lucide:bell",           "#e0414a", "N", false, NavManager.OverlayNotifications, false ),
    };

    // ── THE SYSTEM DOCK (v5) — meta destinations below the grid. IDs
    // double as the icon filenames (ui/icons/pawpad/<id>.svg). Routing is
    // CODE (LaunchDock's switch), not data — the hotload static-data law.
    // Cursor space: grid 0..11, dock 12..15.
    private const int GridCount = 12;
    private static readonly string[] Dock = { "profile", "settings", "guide", "feedback" };
    private const int DockCount = 4;

    // Widget vs destination classification — CODE, not data (see the
    // hotload law above; method bodies are always fresh after a hotload).
    // Widgets (Tier-1 popup toggles) close-and-toggle with no sweep; every
    // other app is a full-screen destination and gets the accent swipe.
    private static bool IsWidgetApp( string id ) => id is "chat" or "radio" or "effects" or "alerts";

    private const int Cols = 3;
    private const int Rows = 4;

    // ── Keyboard cursor (hover == focus, one violet ring) ───────────────
    private int _kb = 0;

    // ── THE LIVING RING (main-menu signature, scaled to the PawPad) ─────
    // One absolutely-positioned bordered div inside .pl-grid that GLIDES
    // between focused icons via CSS left/top/width/height transitions
    // (0.27s signature ease). Position comes from the focused icon's
    // Box.Rect converted to style px (× ScaleFromScreen) RELATIVE to the
    // grid's rect — both rects are flat layout space, and the ring lives
    // inside the same 3D-leaned subtree as the icons, so no perspective
    // compensation is needed (contrast MainMenu, whose root-level cursor
    // must project tilted panels manually).
    //
    // v4.2 FPS LAW (amended): the ring now lives at ROOT level, OUTSIDE
    // the leaned subtree — the menu's own placement. Per-frame writes on
    // it are cheap (they no longer dirty the 3D device), so the liquid
    // ink-lean wave is BACK (imperative Style.Transform, no re-render).
    // The 7fps law still stands for everything INSIDE .pl-device: nothing
    // in the leaned subtree may be dirtied per frame. Rect math stays
    // event-driven (_ringDirty), PLUS a short hold window after open so
    // the ring re-targets while the entrance slide moves the icons.
    private Panel _gridRef;
    private Panel _dockRef;
    private Panel _deviceRef;
    private Panel _ringRef;

    // ── Lean projection (v5, log-proven) — Box.Rect is LAYOUT space
    // (pre-transform): the walkdbg rect log showed pure layout deltas
    // (140px row steps, zero perspective compression), while the paint is
    // projected through .pl-device's lean. The root-level ring must apply
    // the SAME projection or it drifts toward the bottom-left, growing
    // with distance from the transform origin (right center) — ~50px off
    // at the dock live. Constants MUST match the .pl-device scss:
    // perspective(1600px) rotateY(-13deg), origin right center.
    // CALIBRATED, not derived (v5.1): with the geometric 13° constants the
    // ring measured 3px right at SKILLS / 4.5px at QUESTS (bias grows with
    // distance from the origin). A deliberate perturbation (LeanSin +0.030
    // → bias +3.5px) gave the slope; zeroing the original bias lands at
    // LeanSin ≈ 0.200 — the engine's EFFECTIVE lean is ~11.5°, SHALLOWER
    // than the authored 13°. Re-fit if the scss angle/perspective changes:
    // measure ring-vs-tile gaps at two columns, adjust by measured slope.
    private const float LeanPerspective = 1600f;
    private const float LeanCos = 0.97980f;  // cos ~11.5° (fitted)
    private const float LeanSin = 0.20000f;  // sin ~11.5° (fitted)

    // Project a layout-space point (style px, root-local) through the lean.
    // rotateY(-13°): a point dx left of the origin recedes (z = -sin·|dx|),
    // so its projection scale s = p / (p - sin·dx) < 1, pulling it toward
    // the origin's x AND toward the device's vertical center.
    private static Vector2 ProjectLean( float x, float y, float x0, float y0 )
    {
        float dx = x - x0;
        float s = LeanPerspective / ( LeanPerspective - LeanSin * dx );
        return new Vector2( x0 + LeanCos * dx * s, y0 + ( y - y0 ) * s );
    }
    private int _ringL, _ringT, _ringW = 112, _ringH = 112;
    private int _ringWarmup;   // 0/1 = snap to position (no glide), 2 = animate — menu warmup pattern
    private bool _ringDirty;   // event-driven update latch — the v4 fps fix
    private float _ringHoldUntil; // keep re-targeting through the 0.28s entrance slide

    // Ring geometry: 12px box inset = ~8px VISIBLE gap + the 4px border
    // (the menu's inset-10 recipe reads as a 6px gap; the PawPad wants the
    // slightly airier "gap look"). Radius lives in SCSS: icon 22 + gap → 30.
    private const int RingInset = 12;

    // Focus pop — the focused icon lifts toward the player via CSS
    // (translateY(-4px) scale(1.06)). Box.Rect does NOT move with CSS
    // transforms, so the ring must mirror the pop into its target rect
    // manually — the menu's SelectedPop lockstep. These constants MUST
    // match the .pl-app.focused .pl-app-icon transform in the SCSS.
    private const float FocusPopScale = 1.06f;
    private const float FocusPopLift = 6f;   // v5.2: raised so the lift-off-the-planted-shadow reads

    private void UpdateRing()
    {
        // Runs ONLY while _ringDirty (open / focus move pending) — never
        // per-frame. Early returns leave the latch set so the next frame
        // retries until layout yields real rects.
        if ( _gridRef == null ) return;
        var icon = FocusedIconEl();
        if ( icon == null ) return;

        // v5: Box.Rect is LAYOUT space (log-proven — see the lean-projection
        // field comment), so the target rect must be pushed through the
        // device's lean before the root-level ring can wrap the PAINT.
        var ir = icon.Box.Rect;
        var rr = Box.Rect;
        var dr = _deviceRef?.Box.Rect ?? default;
        if ( ir.Width < 1f || rr.Width < 1f || dr.Width < 1f ) return; // not laid out yet — stay dirty, retry

        float sc = ScaleFromScreen;
        if ( sc <= 0.01f || float.IsNaN( sc ) || float.IsInfinity( sc ) ) sc = 1f;

        // Transform origin (right center of the device), root-local style px.
        float x0 = ( dr.Right - rr.Left ) * sc;
        float y0 = ( dr.Top + dr.Height / 2f - rr.Top ) * sc;

        // Project all four corners; the painted tile is a trapezoid, the
        // ring is axis-aligned — take the bounding box.
        float il = ( ir.Left - rr.Left ) * sc, it = ( ir.Top - rr.Top ) * sc;
        float irr = ( ir.Right - rr.Left ) * sc, ib = ( ir.Bottom - rr.Top ) * sc;
        var tl = ProjectLean( il, it, x0, y0 );
        var tr = ProjectLean( irr, it, x0, y0 );
        var bl = ProjectLean( il, ib, x0, y0 );
        var br = ProjectLean( irr, ib, x0, y0 );
        float pL = MathF.Min( tl.x, bl.x ), pR = MathF.Max( tr.x, br.x );
        float pT = MathF.Min( tl.y, tr.y ), pB = MathF.Max( bl.y, br.y );

        // The focused icon ALWAYS wears the pop (focused == the ring's
        // target), so the pop offsets apply unconditionally: scale grows
        // the box around its center, the lift shifts it up.
        float iw = pR - pL, ih = pB - pT;
        float growX = iw * ( FocusPopScale - 1f );
        float growY = ih * ( FocusPopScale - 1f );

        int left = (int)( pL - growX / 2f ) - RingInset;
        int top = (int)( pT - growY / 2f - FocusPopLift ) - RingInset;
        int w = (int)( iw + growX ) + RingInset * 2;
        int h = (int)( ih + growY ) + RingInset * 2;

        bool changed = false;
        if ( left != _ringL || top != _ringT || w != _ringW || h != _ringH )
        {
            if ( WALK_DEBUG ) Log.Info( $"[walkdbg] ring kb={_kb} ir=({ir.Left:F0},{ir.Top:F0},{ir.Width:F0}x{ir.Height:F0}) rr=({rr.Left:F0},{rr.Top:F0}) sc={sc:F3} -> ({left},{top},{w}x{h})" );
            _ringL = left; _ringT = top; _ringW = w; _ringH = h; changed = true;
        }
        if ( _ringWarmup < 2 ) { _ringWarmup++; changed = true; } // snap first 1-2 frames, then glide

        // Sleep the latch once the warmup snaps are done — the CSS
        // transitions carry the glide from here with zero per-frame work.
        _ringDirty = _ringWarmup < 2;

        if ( changed ) StateHasChanged(); // markup position — rare (focus changes), not per-frame
    }

    // The liquid ink-lean — the menu cursor's exact multi-sine (two slow
    // detuned layers per axis, no fast term), at ×0.6 amplitude (full-size
    // degrees read as flailing on a ~112px ring — v3 finding). LEGAL again
    // because the ring is outside the leaned subtree (v4.2): imperative
    // Style.Transform per frame repaints the ring alone, no re-render, no
    // 3D re-composite.
    private void ApplyRingWave()
    {
        if ( _ringRef == null ) return;
        float wt = Time.Now;
        // v5.1 rebalance (user: "too uniform, just shifting left and right"):
        // the menu mix is skewX-heavy, which on a small square ring reads as
        // pure lateral wobble. Cut skewX, raise skewY + rotZ, and add a tiny
        // out-of-phase per-axis breathing (squash/stretch) — the breathing
        // is what makes it read LIQUID instead of metronome.
        float skX = ( 2.0f * MathF.Sin( wt * 2.2f ) + 0.7f * MathF.Sin( wt * 3.5f + 1.1f ) ) * 0.6f;
        float skY = ( 2.3f * MathF.Sin( wt * 1.8f + 1.9f ) + 0.9f * MathF.Sin( wt * 2.9f ) ) * 0.6f;
        float rotZ = ( 1.1f * MathF.Sin( wt * 1.0f ) + 0.5f * MathF.Sin( wt * 2.4f + 0.5f ) ) * 0.6f;
        float brX = 1f + 0.013f * MathF.Sin( wt * 1.35f + 0.7f ) + 0.006f * MathF.Sin( wt * 2.7f );
        float brY = 1f + 0.013f * MathF.Sin( wt * 1.15f + 2.6f ) + 0.006f * MathF.Sin( wt * 2.3f + 1.4f );

        var t = new PanelTransform();
        t.AddRotation( 0f, 0f, rotZ );
        t.AddSkew( skX, skY, 0f );
        t.AddScale( new Vector2( brX, brY ) );
        _ringRef.Style.Transform = t;
    }

    // The focused tile's ICON square, walked from the grid/dock ref each
    // call (by class — survives re-renders; no per-tile @ref array needed).
    // Dock focus (12..15) targets the dock tile itself (it IS the visual).
    private Panel FocusedIconEl()
    {
        if ( _kb >= GridCount )
        {
            if ( _dockRef == null ) return null;
            int want = _kb - GridCount, di = 0;
            foreach ( var tile in _dockRef.Children )
            {
                if ( !tile.HasClass( "pl-dock-app" ) ) continue;
                if ( di++ == want ) return tile;
            }
            return null;
        }

        int row = _kb / Cols, col = _kb % Cols;
        int ri = 0;
        foreach ( var child in _gridRef.Children )
        {
            if ( !child.HasClass( "pl-row" ) ) continue;
            if ( ri++ != row ) continue;
            int ci = 0;
            foreach ( var tile in child.Children )
            {
                if ( !tile.HasClass( "pl-app" ) ) continue;
                if ( ci++ != col ) continue;
                foreach ( var wrap in tile.Children )
                {
                    if ( !wrap.HasClass( "pl-app-iconwrap" ) ) continue;
                    foreach ( var ic in wrap.Children )
                        if ( ic.HasClass( "pl-app-icon" ) ) return ic;
                }
                return null;
            }
            return null;
        }
        return null;
    }

    // (v4: ApplyRingWave is DELETED — see the FPS LAW comment above. If the
    // wave ever comes back, it must live on a ROOT-level element outside
    // the leaned device, like the menu's cursor — never in this subtree.)

    // ── Focus brighten — the focused app's fill lifts toward white.
    // Inline C# swap (instant SNAP), not a CSS overlay: absolute full-cover
    // overlay children paint BEHIND a parent's background-color (engine
    // quirk), so "brighten via white wash div" is a trap here.
    private static readonly Dictionary<string, string> _brightCache = new();

    private static string Brighten( string hex )
    {
        if ( _brightCache.TryGetValue( hex, out var cached ) ) return cached;
        // All accents are "#rrggbb" literals from the registry — parse by hand
        // (no engine API dependency) and lift 18% toward white.
        var result = hex;
        if ( hex != null && hex.Length == 7 && hex[0] == '#' )
        {
            int r = Convert.ToInt32( hex.Substring( 1, 2 ), 16 );
            int g = Convert.ToInt32( hex.Substring( 3, 2 ), 16 );
            int b = Convert.ToInt32( hex.Substring( 5, 2 ), 16 );
            r += (int)( ( 255 - r ) * 0.18f );
            g += (int)( ( 255 - g ) * 0.18f );
            b += (int)( ( 255 - b ) * 0.18f );
            result = $"#{r:x2}{g:x2}{b:x2}";
        }
        _brightCache[hex] = result;
        return result;
    }

    // ── Focus shadow — a hard-edged accent-DARKENED drop shadow under the
    // popped tile (v5.1, user call: the pop should read 3D, like the tile
    // lifts off the glass). Down-left offset matches the shell's own light
    // (the device leans right, light comes from the right). Zero blur =
    // the Persona offset-shadow dialect. Grid is NOT a scroll container,
    // so the colored-shadow-leak rule doesn't apply here.
    private static readonly Dictionary<string, string> _darkCache = new();

    private static string Darken( string hex )
    {
        if ( _darkCache.TryGetValue( hex, out var cached ) ) return cached;
        var result = hex;
        if ( hex != null && hex.Length == 7 && hex[0] == '#' )
        {
            int r = (int)( Convert.ToInt32( hex.Substring( 1, 2 ), 16 ) * 0.38f );
            int g = (int)( Convert.ToInt32( hex.Substring( 3, 2 ), 16 ) * 0.38f );
            int b = (int)( Convert.ToInt32( hex.Substring( 5, 2 ), 16 ) * 0.38f );
            result = $"#{r:x2}{g:x2}{b:x2}";
        }
        _darkCache[hex] = result;
        return result;
    }

    // ── The accent swipe state machine ───────────────────────────────────
    // Idle → SweepIn (220ms, eased translateX from off-right to full cover;
    // ROUTE fires at cover, phone body hides behind the slab) → Covered
    // (30ms hold — the destination's mount frame lands under the slab) →
    // SweepOut (200ms ease-in off the LEFT side, revealing the destination)
    // → Idle. 450ms total input → settled. Interrupt-safe: a new launch
    // re-seeds the slab off-right; a lost @ref kills the phase cleanly.
    private enum FxPhase { Idle, SweepIn, Covered, SweepOut }

    // Diagnostics — VERIFIED live 2026-07-01 22:11 (log: SWEEP-IN → ROUTE →
    // SWEEP-OUT → DONE for all six tabs, correct accents, full-cover slab,
    // widgets correctly NO-sweep). Flip true again if the sweep regresses.
    private const bool SWEEP_DEBUG = false;

    private const float SweepInSeconds = 0.22f;
    private const float CoverHoldSeconds = 0.03f;
    private const float SweepOutSeconds = 0.20f;
    private const float SwipeSkewDeg = -12f;   // the diagonal leading edge (P5 seam dialect)

    private FxPhase _fx = FxPhase.Idle;
    private float _fxT0;
    private string _fxAccent = "#9b6cff";
    private bool _fxRouted;
    private int _fxAppIndex = -1;

    // Slab geometry in STYLE px, computed at launch (Box.Rect screen px ×
    // ScaleFromScreen, +30%/+24% oversize + skew reach — full-screen-guaranteed).
    private float _swW, _swH, _swLeft, _swTop, _swXOff;

    private Panel _swipe;
    private Panel _fxIcon;   // the launched icon mid shoot-out (SweepIn only)

    private bool Shown => IsVisible || _fx != FxPhase.Idle || Time.Now < _closingUntil;

    // ── Flavor chrome ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Clock string is CACHED and refreshed at most once a second (v4 fps
    // hygiene) — BuildHash reads ClockText EVERY frame, and a fresh
    // DateTime.ToString per frame is pure allocation churn for a value
    // that changes once a minute. Delta is sign-checked: Time.Now resets
    // to ~0 each editor session while instance fields can survive hotload.
    private string _clockCache = "";
    private float _clockCheckedAt = -999f;
    private string ClockText
    {
        get
        {
            float dt = Time.Now - _clockCheckedAt;
            if ( _clockCache == "" || dt < 0f || dt > 1f )
            {
                _clockCheckedAt = Time.Now;
                _clockCache = DateTime.Now.ToString( "HH:mm" );
            }
            return _clockCache;
        }
    }
    private string TamerLine
    {
        get
        {
            var t = Beastborne.Core.TamerManager.Instance?.CurrentTamer;
            return t == null ? "TAMER" : $"{t.Name}  ·  LV {t.Level}";
        }
    }

    // ── px-centering by construction (v4.1) ─────────────────────────────
    // Under the leaned subtree text-align is dead (transform-poisoned
    // derived widths — see the labelrow markup comment), so alignment is
    // computed: auto-width span + margin-left from an estimated glyph
    // advance. Tunable constants, calibrated against live captures:
    // Exo2 italic-800 uppercase ≈ 0.72em/char + letter-spacing.
    private const float LabelCharPx = 10.2f;  // 13px font + 0.8 tracking
    private const float NameCharPx = 11.0f;   // 14px font + 1.0 tracking

    // Center within the 160px labelrow.
    private static int LabelPadPx( string label ) =>
        (int)Math.Max( 0f, (160f - label.Length * LabelCharPx) / 2f );

    // Right-align against the avatar: push the name so its right edge
    // lands at the .pl-id 392px mark. Deliberately UNDER-estimates (gap
    // beats overflow — overflow would shove the avatar past the bezel).
    private int NamePadPx() =>
        (int)Math.Max( 0f, 392f - TamerLine.Length * NameCharPx );

    // Avatar — the command bar's exact house pattern (GameHUD): Steam
    // avatar via the avatar: URL when connected, gendered portrait PNG
    // fallback for dev playtests without a real SteamId. Method (not a
    // bare property) — `SteamId` alone collides with the engine TYPE.
    private long GetSteamId() => Connection.Local?.SteamId ?? 0;

    private string GetAvatarImagePath() =>
        Beastborne.Core.TamerManager.Instance?.CurrentTamer?.Gender == Beastborne.Data.TamerGender.Female
            ? "ui/characters/female/female_tamer.png"
            : "ui/characters/male/male_tamer.png";

    // One-shot avatar diagnostic (v4) — the status-row avatar failed to
    // render across two live tests; this logs the EXACT src the markup
    // resolves on the first visible frame so the next session can diagnose
    // from the log if it's still missing.
    private bool _avaLogged;

    // ── Badges (carried over from the command bar's counts) ─────────────
    private int GetBadgeCount( string appId ) => appId switch
    {
        "quests" => Panels.QuestPanel.GetTotalUnclaimedCount(),
        "chat" => ChatPanel.UnreadMessageCount,
        "effects" => ActiveEffectsPanel.TotalEffectCount,
        "alerts" => NotificationPanel.UnreadCount,
        _ => 0,
    };

    private bool HasNewItems() => Beastborne.Core.ItemManager.Instance?.HasNewItems ?? false;

    private string FormatBadge( int n ) => n > 99 ? "99+" : n.ToString();

    // ── Open/close plumbing ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    private void ResetForOpen()
    {
        // Land the cursor on the CURRENT tab's tile (tabs occupy tiles 0-5
        // in NavManager order) so Enter re-launches where you are.
        var idx = NavManager.IndexOf( NavManager.CurrentTab );
        _kb = idx >= 0 ? idx : 0;
        _ringWarmup = 0;   // ring SNAPS to its first position on open, glides thereafter
        _ringDirty = true; // wake the event-driven ring update
        // v4.2: the ring is at root level — it no longer rides the wrap's
        // entrance slide, so keep re-targeting until the icons settle
        // (0.28s slide + margin). The ring's own opacity delay hides the
        // chase; it fades in already on target.
        _ringHoldUntil = Time.Now + 0.4f;
    }

    private void OnBackdropClicked()
    {
        Close();
    }

    private void HoverTile( int i )
    {
        if ( !IsVisible || i == _kb ) return;
        _kb = i;
        _ringDirty = true;
        SoundManager.PlayHover();
    }

    // ── Launch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    private void LaunchIndex( int i )
    {
        if ( i < 0 || i >= GridCount + DockCount ) return;
        if ( i >= GridCount ) { LaunchDock( i - GridCount ); return; }
        var app = Apps[i];
        _kb = i;
        _ringDirty = true;

        if ( !IsWidgetApp( app.Id ) )
        {
            SoundManager.PlayForward();
            StartSwipe( i, app );
        }
        else
        {
            // Widget apps: no sweep — close the phone (Close plays its own
            // popdown), toggle the popup (which plays its own open sound).
            if ( SWEEP_DEBUG ) Log.Info( $"[sweepdbg] widget launch '{app.Id}' — NO sweep by design (Tier-1 popup toggle) t={Time.Now:F3}" );
            Close();
            RouteApp( i );
        }
    }

    // Dock launches are all Tier-1 popups/overlays — no sweep (widget
    // discipline): close the phone, open the destination. Routing lives
    // in code, not data (hotload law).
    private void LaunchDock( int d )
    {
        if ( d < 0 || d >= Dock.Length ) return;
        _kb = GridCount + d;
        Close();
        // Stamp the route latch — these open via panel statics, not
        // NavManager, so without this the same edge-triggered Enter also
        // fires the global open-chat bind (live: chat popped over the
        // freshly-opened dock destination).
        NavManager.MarkRouted();
        switch ( Dock[d] )
        {
            case "profile": NavManager.OpenOverlay( NavManager.OverlayProfile ); break;
            case "settings": OptionsPanel.Show(); break;
            case "guide": Beastborne.UI.Panels.HelpPanel.Show(); break;
            case "feedback": Beastborne.UI.Panels.FeedbackPanel.Show(); break;
        }
    }

    private void RouteApp( int i )
    {
        if ( i < 0 || i >= Apps.Length ) return;
        var app = Apps[i];
        if ( app.IsTab ) NavManager.GoTo( app.RouteId );
        else NavManager.OpenOverlay( app.RouteId );
    }

    // ── The accent swipe ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    private void StartSwipe( int i, PhoneApp app )
    {
        // Screen size in STYLE px. Box.Rect is screen space; ScaleFromScreen
        // converts to local style units (at 1080p scale-1 they're identical
        // — the MainMenu precedent — but the liquid circle under-covered on
        // scaled windows, so v2 converts properly and oversizes on top).
        var r = Box.Rect;
        float sc = ScaleFromScreen;
        if ( sc <= 0.01f || float.IsNaN( sc ) || float.IsInfinity( sc ) ) sc = 1f;
        float w = MathF.Max( r.Width * sc, 320f );
        float h = MathF.Max( r.Height * sc, 180f );

        // Oversized slab, centered on the screen: +30% wide / +24% tall, so
        // the skewed leading edge can never expose a corner at full cover.
        _swW = w * 1.30f;
        _swH = h * 1.24f;
        _swLeft = -( _swW - w ) / 2f;
        _swTop = -( _swH - h ) / 2f;

        // Travel offset: fully off the right edge including the skew reach
        // (skewX shifts the vertical edges by tan(deg) × half-height).
        float skewReach = MathF.Tan( MathF.Abs( SwipeSkewDeg ) * MathF.PI / 180f ) * _swH / 2f;
        _swXOff = ( w - _swLeft ) + skewReach + 24f;

        _fxAccent = app.Accent;
        _fxAppIndex = i;
        _fxRouted = false;
        _fxT0 = Time.Now;
        _fx = FxPhase.SweepIn;   // re-seeding mid-flight IS the interrupt path

        // v5.1 launch beat (user call): the tapped icon SHOOTS OUT left,
        // ahead of the incoming slab — grab its panel now (fresh walk;
        // refs die on hotload and re-renders). Per-frame transform inside
        // the lean is a knowing, TRANSIENT violation of the 7fps law:
        // ~13 frames during SweepIn, then the slab covers everything.
        _fxIcon = FocusedIconEl();

        // Seed the first frame immediately so there's no 1-frame pop.
        if ( _swipe != null ) ApplySwipe( _swipe, _swXOff );
        if ( SWEEP_DEBUG ) Log.Info( $"[sweepdbg] SWEEP-IN '{app.Id}' accent={app.Accent} slab={_swW:F0}x{_swH:F0} at=({_swLeft:F0},{_swTop:F0}) xoff={_swXOff:F0} sc={sc:F2} refBound={_swipe != null} t={Time.Now:F3}" );
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Per-frame swipe step. Everything is TIME-based (not per-frame lerp)
    /// so the mount-stall a tab swap can cause under cover only skips
    /// frames, never changes the total duration — and the freeze lands
    /// while the screen is a solid accent slab, which is the whole point
    /// of routing at full cover.
    /// </summary>
    private void StepFx()
    {
        if ( _fx == FxPhase.Idle ) return;
        var el = _swipe;
        if ( el == null ) { _fx = FxPhase.Idle; return; }

        if ( _fx == FxPhase.SweepIn )
        {
            float u = Math.Clamp( ( Time.Now - _fxT0 ) / SweepInSeconds, 0f, 1f );
            float e = 1f - MathF.Pow( 1f - u, 3f );   // ease-out cubic — fast attack, soft landing
            ApplySwipe( el, _swXOff * ( 1f - e ) );

            // The launched icon rockets left ahead of the slab. EASE-OUT,
            // not ease-in: the slab sweeps right-to-left and swallows the
            // phone almost immediately, so the icon only reads if it leaps
            // in the first ~100ms (live-verified — the ease-in version was
            // fully covered before it moved).
            if ( _fxIcon != null )
            {
                float li = 1f - ( 1f - u ) * ( 1f - u );
                var lt = new PanelTransform();
                lt.AddTranslate( Length.Pixels( -340f * li ), Length.Pixels( 0f ), Length.Pixels( 0f ) );
                lt.AddScale( 1f + 0.12f * li );
                _fxIcon.Style.Transform = lt;
            }

            if ( u >= 1f )
            {
                // Under full cover: return the icon to rest (unseen) so the
                // grid is intact next open, and stop the per-frame writes.
                if ( _fxIcon != null ) { _fxIcon.Style.Transform = null; _fxIcon = null; }
                if ( !_fxRouted )
                {
                    _fxRouted = true;
                    // Full cover: hide the phone body instantly behind the
                    // slab — no close animation (it would never be seen) and
                    // the modal releases so the destination owns input.
                    IsVisible = false;
                    _closingUntil = 0f;
                    if ( SWEEP_DEBUG ) Log.Info( $"[sweepdbg] ROUTE '{Apps[_fxAppIndex].Id}' at full cover t={Time.Now:F3}" );
                    RouteApp( _fxAppIndex );
                }
                _fx = FxPhase.Covered;
                _fxT0 = Time.Now;
            }
        }
        else if ( _fx == FxPhase.Covered )
        {
            // Held at full cover for a beat — the destination's first-layout
            // frame lands here, invisible behind the slab.
            ApplySwipe( el, 0f );
            if ( Time.Now - _fxT0 >= CoverHoldSeconds )
            {
                if ( SWEEP_DEBUG ) Log.Info( $"[sweepdbg] SWEEP-OUT begins t={Time.Now:F3}" );
                _fx = FxPhase.SweepOut;
                _fxT0 = Time.Now;
            }
        }
        else if ( _fx == FxPhase.SweepOut )
        {
            float v = Math.Clamp( ( Time.Now - _fxT0 ) / SweepOutSeconds, 0f, 1f );
            float e = v * v * v;   // ease-in cubic — the slab accelerates off
            ApplySwipe( el, -_swXOff * e );

            if ( v >= 1f )
            {
                if ( SWEEP_DEBUG ) Log.Info( $"[sweepdbg] DONE — slab cleared, back to Idle t={Time.Now:F3}" );
                _fx = FxPhase.Idle;
                _fxAppIndex = -1;
                ClearSwipeStyles( el );
                StateHasChanged();
            }
        }
    }

    // Re-asserts position + size + transform + opacity EVERY frame
    // (rebuild-proof — the PlaneTween HoldUntil lesson: one-shot style
    // writes get wiped by re-renders; per-frame writes survive anything).
    private void ApplySwipe( Panel el, float x )
    {
        el.Style.Left = Length.Pixels( _swLeft );
        el.Style.Top = Length.Pixels( _swTop );
        el.Style.Width = Length.Pixels( _swW );
        el.Style.Height = Length.Pixels( _swH );
        var t = new PanelTransform();
        t.AddTranslate( Length.Pixels( x ), Length.Pixels( 0f ), Length.Pixels( 0f ) );
        t.AddSkew( SwipeSkewDeg, 0f, 0f );
        el.Style.Transform = t;
        el.Style.Opacity = 1f;
    }

    // Return the slab to its CSS rest state (parked 100×100, opacity 0).
    private void ClearSwipeStyles( Panel el )
    {
        el.Style.Left = null;
        el.Style.Top = null;
        el.Style.Width = null;
        el.Style.Height = null;
        el.Style.Transform = null;
        el.Style.Opacity = null;
    }

    // ── Per-frame — s&box auto-ticks Panel-derived razor components ──────
    public override void Tick()
    {
        base.Tick();
        Instance = this;   // re-asserted every frame — hotload can never strand a stale instance

        // Session-restart sanity (the RoutedThisFrame lesson): statics survive
        // across editor play sessions while Time.Now resets to ~0, so a stale
        // FUTURE _closingUntil from the previous session would hold Shown true
        // (root parked at left: 0) for as long as that session ran. The max
        // legit window is 0.18s — anything further out is stale; clear it.
        if ( _closingUntil > Time.Now + 1f ) _closingUntil = 0f;

        // Leaving the game (back to main menu) force-closes the phone —
        // otherwise the static IsVisible would hold UIModalState.AnyModalOpen
        // true over the menu forever.
        if ( Beastborne.Core.GameManager.Instance?.IsInGame != true )
        {
            if ( IsVisible ) { IsVisible = false; _closingUntil = 0f; }
            if ( _fx != FxPhase.Idle )
            {
                // Abandon the flight AND clear the slab's inline styles —
                // a stale opacity-1 cover would otherwise flash on next open.
                if ( SWEEP_DEBUG ) Log.Info( $"[sweepdbg] ABANDONED — left game mid-sweep t={Time.Now:F3}" );
                _fx = FxPhase.Idle;
                _fxAppIndex = -1;
                if ( _swipe != null ) ClearSwipeStyles( _swipe );
                if ( _fxIcon != null ) { _fxIcon.Style.Transform = null; _fxIcon = null; }
            }
            return;
        }

        StepFx();

        if ( !IsVisible ) return;

        // One-shot avatar-source diagnostic (v4 — see field comment).
        if ( !_avaLogged )
        {
            _avaLogged = true;
            var sid = GetSteamId();
            Log.Info( $"[pawpad] avatar src = '{( sid > 0 ? $"avatar:{sid}" : GetAvatarImagePath() )}' (steamId={sid}, ref-in-dom={_ringRef != null})" );
        }

        // The living ring — rect math stays EVENT-DRIVEN (open/focus/
        // entrance-hold), but the WAVE runs per frame now that the ring is
        // outside the leaned subtree (v4.2 — imperative transform only,
        // no re-render). Sign-checked hold: Time.Now resets per session
        // while this instance's field can survive hotload.
        float holdDt = _ringHoldUntil - Time.Now;
        if ( holdDt > 1f ) _ringHoldUntil = 0f;            // stale stamp from a prior session
        else if ( holdDt > 0f ) _ringDirty = true;         // entrance slide still moving the icons
        if ( _ringDirty ) UpdateRing();
        ApplyRingWave();
        if ( WALK_DEBUG && ( Input.Pressed( "Backward" ) || Input.Pressed( "Forward" ) ) )
            Log.Info( $"[walkdbg] tick gate: top={UIModalState.IsTopModal( "PhoneLauncher" )} chatfocus={ChatPanel.IsChatFocused}" );
        if ( !UIModalState.IsTopModal( "PhoneLauncher" ) ) return;
        if ( ChatPanel.IsChatFocused ) return;

        HandleKeyboard();
    }

    // Diagnostics (v5) — root-caused and VERIFIED 2026-07-02: the "dead
    // vertical walk" was a partial hotload wedge (markup swapped, old
    // method body kept running — the "worker threads" stall); the ring
    // drift was Box.Rect being LAYOUT space (fixed via ProjectLean).
    // Flip true if the walk or ring regresses.
    private const bool WALK_DEBUG = false;

    private void HandleKeyboard()
    {
        if ( WALK_DEBUG && ( Input.Pressed( "Forward" ) || Input.Pressed( "Backward" ) || Input.Pressed( "Left" ) || Input.Pressed( "Right" ) ) )
            Log.Info( $"[walkdbg] press F={Input.Pressed( "Forward" )} B={Input.Pressed( "Backward" )} L={Input.Pressed( "Left" )} R={Input.Pressed( "Right" )} kb={_kb} routed={NavManager.RoutedThisFrame}" );
        // Same-frame double-fire guard: Input.Pressed is edge-triggered and
        // reports true to EVERY handler this frame. The Slot8 press that just
        // OPENED the phone (via GameHUD → NavManager) must not also be read
        // here as "close"; ditto any direct-route key GameHUD handled.
        if ( NavManager.RoutedThisFrame ) return;

        // Close — Q ("Menu"), Escape, or Slot8 (the key that opened it: true toggle).
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Menu" ) || Input.Pressed( "Escape" ) || Input.Pressed( "Slot8" ) )
        {
            Close();
            return;
        }

        // Direct-route keys — number keys + the widget letters, same map as
        // the command bar so muscle memory transfers 1:1.
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot1" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 0 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot2" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 1 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot3" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 2 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot4" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 3 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot5" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 4 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot6" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 5 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot7" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 6 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot9" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 7 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Chat" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 8 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Reload" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 9 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "View" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 10 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Notifications" ) ) { LaunchIndex( 11 ); return; }
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Slot0" ) ) { LaunchIndex( GridCount ); return; } // 0 = Profile (old-bar muscle memory)

        // Grid + dock walk — WASD, wrapping both axes. The dock is a 5th
        // row with 4 columns; horizontal wraps stay within the row you're
        // on, vertical crossings map columns proportionally (3-wide grid ↔
        // 4-wide dock).
        bool onDock = _kb >= GridCount;
        int next = -1;
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Left" ) )
        {
            next = onDock
                ? GridCount + ( ( _kb - GridCount + DockCount - 1 ) % DockCount )
                : ( _kb / Cols ) * Cols + ( ( _kb % Cols + Cols - 1 ) % Cols );
        }
        else if ( Input.Pressed( "Right" ) )
        {
            next = onDock
                ? GridCount + ( ( _kb - GridCount + 1 ) % DockCount )
                : ( _kb / Cols ) * Cols + ( ( _kb % Cols + 1 ) % Cols );
        }
        else if ( Input.Pressed( "Forward" ) ) // up
        {
            if ( onDock ) next = ( Rows - 1 ) * Cols + DockColToGridCol( _kb - GridCount );
            else if ( _kb / Cols == 0 ) next = GridCount + GridColToDockCol( _kb % Cols ); // wrap up → dock
            else next = _kb - Cols;
        }
        else if ( Input.Pressed( "Backward" ) ) // down
        {
            if ( onDock ) next = GridColToGridIndexRow0( _kb - GridCount ); // wrap down → grid top
            else if ( _kb / Cols == Rows - 1 ) next = GridCount + GridColToDockCol( _kb % Cols );
            else next = _kb + Cols;
        }

        if ( next >= 0 )
        {
            if ( WALK_DEBUG ) Log.Info( $"[walkdbg] moved {_kb} -> {next}" );
            _kb = next;
            _ringDirty = true;
            SoundManager.PlayHover();
            return;
        }

        // Column mapping between the 3-wide grid and 4-wide dock: keep the
        // crossing feeling straight-down/straight-up (proportional, rounded).
        static int GridColToDockCol( int c ) => c switch { 0 => 0, 1 => 2, _ => 3 };
        static int DockColToGridCol( int d ) => d switch { 0 => 0, 1 => 1, 2 => 1, _ => 2 };
        static int GridColToGridIndexRow0( int d ) => DockColToGridCol( d );

        // Launch — Enter or Space (the canonical confirm pair).
        if ( Input.Pressed( "Enter" ) || Input.Pressed( "Jump" ) )
        {
            LaunchIndex( _kb );
        }
    }

    protected override int BuildHash()
    {
        return HashCode.Combine(
            HashCode.Combine( IsVisible, Shown, (int)_fx, _kb, _fxAccent, GetSteamId() ),
            HashCode.Combine(
                GetBadgeCount( "quests" ),
                GetBadgeCount( "chat" ),
                GetBadgeCount( "effects" ),
                GetBadgeCount( "alerts" ),
                HasNewItems(),
                ClockText ),
            // The living ring's markup-driven geometry — without these the
            // panel never repaints a focus glide (missing-BuildHash trap).
            HashCode.Combine( _ringL, _ringT, _ringW, _ringH, _ringWarmup ) );
    }
}
